Thanks.&nbsp; I will, or at least I&#39;ll try to.Anyway, the first run against Ambuscade at Rook City took me four tries.&nbsp; I&#39;ve never done well against Frenchy, especially on advanced; too many tricks up his sleeve prevent me from doing what I want.&nbsp; That and Rook City foiled me the first three times, but on the fourth I finally got him.&nbsp; Fixer kept moving weapons and styles in and out (because he usually blew them up immediately), while Expat kept a steady stream of damage going with her shotgun, which she got early.&nbsp; Nightmist used her necklace to keep her head above water.&nbsp; Two Sonic Mines slowed me down and Ambuscade&#39;s Explosive Launcher threatened to take us all out.&nbsp; Not quite, though, as Expatriette got in two shotgun blasts and an RPG launch for the win.&nbsp; Whew!&nbsp; Forgive me, but that wore me out.But next, we&#39;ll have the Gloomweaver underwater.

[/quote]
Fun fact -- while its destruction is resolving, the Sonic Mine still counts as a target. You can have Nightmist redirect its damage into itself and keep it from harming anyone.
